🩺 Healthcare Utilization & Flu Vaccination Analysis
(Python • Pandas • NumPy • Matplotlib • Seaborn • Scikit-learn)

This project explores healthcare encounter patterns, vaccination behaviour, and demographic insights using two real-world synthetic datasets:

Healthcare Demo Data (2022) – Main dataset

Flu Shot 2019 Survey Data – Secondary dataset

The analysis includes interactive dashboards, data visualizations, and a machine-learning model predicting flu vaccination status.
Designed as a LinkedIn/GitHub portfolio project, it highlights strong EDA, visualization, and modeling skills.

📌 Project Structure
1. Healthcare Demo Data (Primary Dashboard + ML Model)

This dataset contains information about:

Patient demographics

Encounter types (inpatient, outpatient, emergency)

Claim costs

Payer categories

Covid status

Flu vaccination status for 2022

Key insights covered in the dashboard:

Monthly encounter trends

Average claim cost by payer

Cost distribution by encounter class

Flu 2022 vaccination patterns across:

Age

Race

Encounter class

Covid status

KDE age distributions for flu vaccination patterns

Machine Learning Component

A Random Forest Classifier predicts whether a patient received a flu shot in 2022, using:

Age

Race

Encounter class

Payer category

Covid status

Outputs include:

Classification report

ROC curve

Feature importance analysis

📌 2. Flu Shot 2019 Dataset (Secondary Mini-Dashboard)

This dataset is used to build a smaller, supporting dashboard analyzing:

Overall flu shot uptake in 2019

Coverage by:

Age band

Gender

Race

This adds depth to the project by showing historical vaccination behavior.

🧠 Why Two Dashboards?

The datasets cannot be merged because patient IDs and features do not match.
However, both contribute to a cohesive storyline:

“How demographics and healthcare encounters relate to flu vaccination behavior across years.”

So both dashboards are included in the same notebook but analyzed separately.

